hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2910","If Shahm bin Al-Jarud is among those whose narration is acceptable for evidence (i.e., his hadith is reliable), then this narration is valid."
"2911","###\n Ahmad bin Abi Al-Harb Al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abdur-Rahim, on the authority of Shahm bin Al-Jarud, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father (Abdullah bin Umar), who said: \Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) gifted a noble she-camel (Najiba) for which he had been offered three hundred dinars. He came to the Prophet ("""""
